{"availability":"available","full":"Phoenix6001/SmartZoom","name":"SmartZoom","description":"macOS smart zoom for Windows: press a mouse button or shortcut and the paragraph, image or table under the cursor fills the window; press again to snap back. Works in Chromium browsers, Firefox, Word, Excel and PDF readers with no extensions. Tray app, .NET 10, MIT.","category":"Productivity","language":"C#","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T07:05:34Z","updated":"2026-10-08T14:48:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://smartzoom.pages.dev","topics":["accessibility","dotnet","low-vision","magnifier","productivity","smart-zoom","tray-app","windows","wpf","zoom"],"demo":"https://smartzoom.pages.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:03.487Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:03.487Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:03.487Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:07.974Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T15:37:03.487Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Bringing macOS's smart zoom to Windows. Press a mouse button and the application under the cursor zooms its content in on whatever you are pointing at, and brings it to the middle of the window — by the amount you choose in a browser, or to fit the paragraph, table or block of cells in Word and Excel. Press again to return to exactly where you were.","Website: smartzoom.pages.dev · Download: SmartZoom-setup.exe (always the latest release)","Windows has no system gesture for this, so SmartZoom is a small tray app that captures a mouse or keyboard trigger and routes it to a per-application zoom strategy:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Phoenix6001/SmartZoom/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dfeda1cb19e68dd36e9ebbffdc392ae19170da46a08e6a07f8f3137cfa804d72","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T01:11:30.247Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:11:30.247Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"te